From: TheGammaSqueeze (GammaOS), azahar-nano
Subject: Never leave out an offscreen draw while its pipeline compiles

GammaOSNextDistribution-14 e842af2339c (2026-10-24), the core's part
(gammaos/emulators/azahar-nano), unchanged:

With a cold shader cache the hybrid path skips draws until their pipeline
is built. That is fine for a screen, which is redrawn every frame, but a
pass into a texture that the game composes once is never repeated: Pokemon
Sun layers a Pokemon's skin into its texture when a scene loads, and the
skipped draws left the Pokemon plain red until the texture was rebuilt.
Display transfers to either screen now record the memory they read from
(240x400 top, 240x320 bottom), and a draw whose colour target lies outside
all of it waits for its software path pipeline instead of being skipped,
like the bottom screen rule already did. A target a screen reads from,
even partly, keeps the fallback, as does everything before the first
screen image. Waiting only costs when the pipeline is new.

The hybrid path is on here too (gammaos_hybrid_shaders, settings.h).

